<title>INDIA: India Thomas Cook 1996 net up 25.6 pct.</title>
<headline>India Thomas Cook 1996 net up 25.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     136.5  vs  108.6</p>
<p>    Income		   524.7  vs  432.6</p>
<p>    Other income	    17.1  vs   13.2</p>
<p>    Expenditure	    270.5  vs  219.9</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   8.6  vs    8.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    16.3  vs   14.2</p>
<p>    Tax			110.0  vs   94.0</p>
<p>Note: Travel and leisure firm Thomas Cook (India) Ltd said in a statement its 1996 earnings per share was 26 rupees. It said it set a dividend of 5.5 rupees a share. The firm earlier announced a bonus issue of two shares for every three held.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
